COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from DA454064.1, U88967.1, M93426.1,
            DA101746.1, CX872418.1 and CX868991.1.
            This sequence is a reference standard in the RefSeqGene project.
            
            On Nov 24, 2018 this sequence version replaced NM_002851.2.
            
            Summary: This gene encodes a member of the receptor protein
            tyrosine phosphatase family. Expression of this gene is restricted
            to the central nervous system (CNS), and it may be involved in the
            regulation of specific developmental processes in the CNS.
            Alternatively spliced transcript variants encoding different
            isoforms have been described for this gene. [provided by RefSeq,
            May 2011].
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
